                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2607.28611/2607.28611v1/x6.png",
                "caption": "Figure 4:Conceptual comparison of local-mixing designs in vision modality.Conventional 1D short convolution is paired with multi-axis scanning for vision modeling, whereas our modality-aware short convolution models spatial-temporal locality under a single scan pattern",
                "position": 836
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2607.28611/2607.28611v1/x7.png",
                "caption": "Figure 5:Expert load balance during training.We plot the batch-levelMaxVio\\operatorname{MaxVio}(Eq.22), averaged over all MoE layers. With auxiliary-loss-free balancing,MaxVio\\operatorname{MaxVio}stays around0.50.5throughout training; without it,MaxVio\\operatorname{MaxVio}rises above55, approaching the collapse bound ofN/K−1=6N/K-1=6.",
